From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 06:45:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: sec_config: allow QMI service 703 (lge_ims)

VoLTE audio on this device runs on the modem, not through AudioTrack: MMPF
creates a media session on the modem and hands it the IMS PDN address, both
over LG's private QMI service 703 (0x2bf). Every send failed --

  IPC_RTR: msm_ipc_router_send_to: permission failure for Framework
  [mmpf_cpif_send_msg] send_msg_sync error: -16
  AudioAdaptor::GetIPAddrOfCP() Error[21]

-- because sec_config grants IPC-router access to services 1-511, 704 and
4097 but not 703, and the router denies a rule-less service to everything but
root while com.lge.ims runs as radio. Without the modem media session there is
no RTP, so the framework's 5s RTP-inactivity threshold tore down every
answered call after ~20s and Ims4 then dropped registration.

With the rule, GetIPAddrOfCP returns the address and the audio media session
reaches LIVE. Note the rule must be programmed before the modem registers the
service -- running irsc_util by hand after boot changes nothing, which is why
this belongs in the file init.qcom.rc already feeds it.

---
 configs/permissions/sec_config | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/configs/permissions/sec_config b/configs/permissions/sec_config
index b6eed59c..87054844 100644
--- a/configs/permissions/sec_config
+++ b/configs/permissions/sec_config
@@ -327,3 +327,12 @@
 57:4294967295:1000
 /* Allow VSS GNSS service to be used by system and net_raw processes */
 704:4294967295:1000:3004
+/* LG lge_ims (QMI service 703 / 0x2bf): com.lge.ims needs it for the modem-side media
+   session that actually carries VoLTE audio -- MMPF_CP_IF::createMediaSession tunnels
+   msg 0x060c over it, and AudioAdaptor::GetIPAddrOfCP asks the modem for the IMS PDN
+   address the same way. LG shipped rules for 1-511, 704 and 4097 and omitted this one,
+   so the MSM IPC router denied every send (IPC_RTR: msm_ipc_router_send_to: permission
+   failure) to anything but root: no modem media session, no RTP, and the framework's
+   RTP-inactivity timer killed each answered call after ~20s. The rule has to exist before
+   the modem registers the service, which is why irsc_util runs from init.qcom.rc. */
+703:4294967295:1000:1001:3004
